# {{project.name}} — AI Workflow

> **AI Steering File** — Kiro workflow adapter.
> The workflow lives in OpenSpec. This file maps it for Kiro.

## Canonical Workflow Entry Point

**Read `openspec/AGENTS.md` before starting any task.**

That file contains:
- The full agent roster and their responsibilities
- The workflow table (Discover → Plan → Implement → Troubleshoot)
- Archetype-specific rules and constraints
- Links to all skill playbooks

## Workflow Summary

| Phase | Agent | Skill Playbook | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| Discover | Discover Agent | `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/discovery.md` | `openspec/changes/discoveries/DISC-###.md` |
| Plan | Plan Agent | `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/planning.md` | `openspec/changes/<mvp>/proposal.md` |
| Implement | Implement Agent | `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/implementation.md` | Source code + updated tracker |
| Troubleshoot | Troubleshoot Agent | `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/troubleshooting.md` | `openspec/changes/bugs/BUG-###.md` |

## How Kiro Should Execute Workflow Phases

### Starting a Discovery
Instruct Kiro: *"Run the Discover workflow for [feature]"*
Kiro reads `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/discovery.md` and writes output to `openspec/changes/discoveries/`.

### Starting a Plan
Instruct Kiro: *"Plan [feature] based on DISC-###"*
Kiro reads `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/planning.md` and writes a proposal to `openspec/changes/`.

### Implementing a Change
Instruct Kiro: *"Implement proposal from [mvp path]"*
Kiro reads `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/implementation.md` and applies the approved proposal layer-by-layer:
Common → Domain → Application → Infrastructure → Presentation.

### Troubleshooting
Instruct Kiro: *"Troubleshoot [issue]"*
Kiro reads `openspec/specs/workflow/skills/troubleshooting.md`. No source changes without a bug proposal.

## Spec Output Paths

Kiro's built-in `.kiro/specs/` directory is **not used** in this project. All outputs must follow the OpenSpec path structure:

| Output | Path |
|---|---|
| Discovery document | `openspec/changes/discoveries/DISC-###.md` |
| MVP planning folder | `openspec/changes/<mvp-name>/` |
| Proposal / design | `openspec/changes/<mvp-name>/proposal.md` |
| Task list | `openspec/changes/<mvp-name>/tasks.md` |
| Bug report | `openspec/changes/bugs/BUG-###.md` |

**Never create or write files under `.kiro/specs/`.** If Kiro prompts to create a spec folder, redirect the output to the matching path above.

## Kiro-Specific Notes

- Kiro does **not** have slash commands. Use natural-language instructions referencing the phase names above.
- Copilot users use `.github/prompts/` for the same workflow. Both tools read the same OpenSpec skills.
- If a Copilot agent exists in `.github/agents/`, the equivalent Kiro behavior is triggered via the instructions above.
